Feature: The computer commander
  A computer can command a team. It looks at the map of its team once each second, and it gives
  each drone an order. It sends one drone to each tower that its team does not hold. It matches
  the free drones to the towers by the time that a drone needs to win a tower. That time is the
  flight, and the capture at the weight of the drone, for each point that the tower gives. The
  pair that wins soonest comes first. A drone does not go to a tower if its battery cannot last
  the flight, the capture and the way home. A drone keeps its order until its team holds the
  tower.

  When drones of the two teams circle a tower, the drone that arrived later is often behind:
  the control is on the side of the other team. A drone that is behind at a contested tower for
  10 s gives up. It goes to a tower that no drone of its team is sent to. If every tower has a
  drone already, it joins the nearest tower that its team does not hold. It does not come back
  for 30 s. The heavy drone goes to the spire at the start. Thus two commanders do not stop each other at every tower.

  When the commander sees an enemy drone within 120 m of a tower that its team holds, it defends
  the tower first. That is two circles out: an enemy drone that circles the next tower is not a
  danger. It sends the drone that is nearest to the tower. The commander uses only the map of its
  team. It does not see an enemy drone in the fog, but it keeps a guess of where the drone is.
  [[What a team believes about the enemy]] tells how.

  The commander also thinks ahead. Every 5 s it plays the game forward 45 s in a small model.
  The enemy drones in the model are guesses from its belief. It tries to send each free drone to
  each other tower. It makes the change that gives most points, if the gain is more than 2
  points. Thus it does not send a drone to a tower where the enemy has more drones than the
  team can bring.

  Expectation: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    Each tower goes to the drone that wins it soonest.
    Blue holds its home tower, so four towers get a drone: the west, the centre, the east and
    the Red home tower. A team has five drones, so the one that is left over joins the nearest
    of them.

    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the towers with a Blue drone on the way are 4

  Expectation: At the start, the heavy drone goes to the spire
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    The heavy drone counts for two drones at a tower. The commander sends it to the spire, the
    tower that gives most points, when the team does not hold the spire and no drone is on it.

    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the fourth Blue drone is take the centre tower

  Expectation: The commander defends a tower that an enemy drone comes near
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    A tower that the team holds comes first. The other drones go on to the neutral towers.

    Given the Red scout is near the Blue home tower
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the second Blue drone is take the Blue home tower

  Expectation: A drone that is behind at a contested tower goes somewhere else
    Given the control of the west tower is -20 %
    And the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the computer commander of Blue plays for 15 seconds
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the centre tower

  Expectation: The commander does not keep a drone at a tower that the enemy holds with two drones
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    The west tower is Red's, and two Red drones circle it. One Blue drone cannot take it. The
    commander thinks ahead and sends the drone to a free tower. Here that is the east tower.

    Given the west tower is held by Red
    And the control of the west tower is -100 %
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 2
    And the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the first Blue drone is 190 m from the centre tower
    When the computer commander of Blue plays for 15 seconds
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the east tower

  Expectation: The commander sends a drone with a low battery home
    Overrides: At the start, the commander sends a drone to each neutral tower
    The commander sends a drone home when its battery is down to 60 s, and the time to fly home,
    and 15 s more. The drone goes back to work when its battery is 90 % full.

    Given the batteries are on
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 80 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the computer commander of Blue decides
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is go home
